3. Check for Even or Odd Number (Control Flow)This program uses a conditional if-else statement along with the modulus operator (%) to evaluate if a number is even or odd.javapublic class EvenOddCheck {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int number = 29;

        // Condition checking if the remainder is zero when divided by 2
        if (number % 2 == 0) {
            System.out.println(number + " is an even number.");
        } else {
            System.out.println(number + " is an odd number.");
        }
    }
}
Use code with caution.4. Reverse a String (String Manipulation)This sample code shows how to manipulate strings by reversing a string using a loop.javapublic class ReverseString {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String original = "Java Programming";
        String reversed = "";
        
        // Loop backwards through the string
        for (int i = original.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            reversed += original.charAt(i);
        }
        
        System.out.println("Original: " + original);
        System.out.println("Reversed: " + reversed);
    }
}



